---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import myAccount from '../../assets/images/my-account.png';
import paymentPortal from '../../assets/images/payment-portal.png';
import qtbMotor from '../../assets/images/QTB-motor.png';
import logIn from '../../assets/images/log-in.png';
import raaWebsite from '../../assets/images/raa-website.png';
import raaBanner from '../../assets/images/raa-banner.png';
import raaHoliday from '../../assets/images/raa-holiday.png';
import uofaBanner from '../../assets/images/uofa-banner.png';
import uofaSubpage from '../../assets/images/uofa-subpage.png';
import uofaMobileMenu from '../../assets/images/uofa-mobile-global-menu.png';
import f1a from '../../assets/images/freelance-1a.png';
import f1b from '../../assets/images/freelance-1b.png';
import f1c from '../../assets/images/freelance-1c.png';
import f2a from '../../assets/images/freelance-2a.png';
import f2b from '../../assets/images/freelance-2b.png';
import f2c from '../../assets/images/freelance-2c.png';
import f3a from '../../assets/images/freelance-3a.png';
import f3b from '../../assets/images/freelance-3b.png';
import f4a from '../../assets/images/freelance-4a.png';
---
<Layout title="UI Design | Andrew Smith" description="UI design across digital products, web, mobile, responsive design, and two decades of freelance client work.">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <div class="case-page">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main id="main-content">
      <section class="case-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow"><a class="breadcrumb-link" href="/portfolio/work">Work</a><span class="breadcrumb-separator">/</span><span>UI Design</span></p>
        <h1 class="display-title">UI design across digital products , web, mobile, and responsive.</h1>
        <p class="hero-text">UI design is not what the interface looks like. It is how every decision about layout, hierarchy, component choice, colour, spacing, and interaction adds up to an experience that either earns a user's confidence or quietly erodes it. The screenshots below show finished product across a range of digital contexts , each one the result of research, testing, and iteration against a design system.</p>
        <p class="hero-text">The technical background matters here. Before working in UX, the tools were HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. That means conversations with engineers about implementation constraints, decisions about what to build versus what to pull from the component library, and handover documents that a developer can actually use , are all informed by having done that work on the other side.</p>
        <p class="hero-text">AI is now part of the UI design process too. Figma plugins for accessibility checking, AI-assisted spec generation, and prototype scanning tools that create realistic test environments from live products , all reducing the overhead of documentation and validation so more time goes to the work that requires judgment.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="meta-strip">
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Organisations</p><p class="meta-value">Multiple, plus freelance</p></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Role</p><p class="meta-value">Senior UX Design Lead</p></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Scope</p><p class="meta-value">Web, mobile, native app, responsive</p></div>
      </section>

      <section class="lead-image-section">
        <Image class="lead-image" src={myAccount} alt="Member portal dashboard showing product management and account details" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>

      <section class="summary-section">
        <p class="section-kicker">Authenticated Products</p>
        <h2>Designing for members who are logged in , where the stakes are higher.</h2>
        <div class="summary-main">
          <p>Authenticated products are harder to design than marketing pages. The user has a real account, real data, and real expectations. The interface needs to serve multiple product types in one place, handle complex state conditions gracefully, and work accessibly across every device size and assistive technology.</p>
          <p>Insurance quote flows, payment portals, and identity management are all technically complex interactions where a small UX failure , a confusing error message, a missing confirmation, a form that loses entered data , has a real cost to the user and the business. Getting these right requires research, testing, and iteration. Not just craft.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="img-pair-section">
        <div class="img-pair">
          <Image class="pair-image" src={qtbMotor} alt="Multi-step insurance quote flow with progressive disclosure and contextual guidance" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080]} sizes="50vw"/>
          <Image class="pair-image" src={paymentPortal} alt="Payment portal with clear payment method selection and member recognition" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080]} sizes="50vw"/>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="editorial-section">
        <div class="section-rail"><p class="section-kicker">Travel & Booking</p></div>
        <div class="story-block">
          <p>Multi-product booking experiences are a particular UI challenge. Flights, stays, holidays, cruises, car hire, and attractions each have different data models, different decision flows, and different user mental models , but they need to feel like one coherent product. The design system is what makes that possible without starting from scratch for each product type.</p>
          <p>Everything here is responsive across all device sizes, following a mobile-first approach that treats the small-screen experience as the baseline rather than the afterthought.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={raaBanner} alt="Travel booking platform shown across desktop, tablet, and mobile" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={raaHoliday} alt="Holiday detail page with itinerary information, pricing, and booking" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>

      <section class="editorial-section">
        <div class="section-rail"><p class="section-kicker">Identity & Website</p></div>
        <div class="story-block">
          <p>A login screen is the first moment of trust in an authenticated product. Get it wrong: too many fields, confusing error states, unclear recovery paths , and users call the contact centre instead of completing what they came to do. The website homepage serves a different challenge: a high-traffic entry point that needs to route multiple audiences to multiple products without overwhelming anyone.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="img-pair-section">
        <div class="img-pair">
          <Image class="pair-image" src={raaWebsite} alt="Website homepage showing navigation hierarchy and member value proposition" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080]} sizes="50vw"/>
          <Image class="pair-image" src={logIn} alt="Login screen with clear email entry and accessible layout" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080]} sizes="50vw"/>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="editorial-section">
        <div class="section-rail"><p class="section-kicker">University of Adelaide</p></div>
        <div class="story-block">
          <p>Five years as UX designer and front-end developer on a large-scale university website rebuild,esigning the interfaces and building them simultaneously on a custom Drupal CMS. The styleguide-driven development approach meant that design decisions made once propagated automatically across every team building on the same codebase. Consistency as a property of the system, not a property of vigilance.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={uofaBanner} alt="University website shown across desktop, tablet, and mobile, responsive design" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="img-pair-section">
        <div class="img-pair">
          <Image class="pair-image" src={uofaSubpage} alt="University research institutes subpage showing navigation, typography, and content hierarchy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080]} sizes="50vw"/>
          <Image class="pair-image-constrained" src={uofaMobileMenu} alt="University mobile global navigation menu" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080]} sizes="50vw"/>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="freelance-section">
        <p class="section-kicker">Freelance UI, UX & Front-End Development</p>
        <h2>Twenty years of client work, designed, built, and shipped.</h2>
        <p class="freelance-intro">Before working in-house, and alongside it, the work was freelance, building websites end to end for clients across e-commerce, health, fitness, and hospitality. Project management, client relationship, design, development, and launch. Every part of the process owned by one person. A sample below.</p>
        <div class="freelance-scroll">
          <div class="freelance-track">
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f1a} alt="PALI Footwear homepage, Shopify e-commerce" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f1b} alt="PALI Footwear product listing page" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f1c} alt="PALI Footwear product detail page" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f2a} alt="Chaircovers Over All homepage, event hire e-commerce" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f2b} alt="Chaircovers Over All product catalogue" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f2c} alt="Chaircovers Over All product detail" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f3a} alt="Graceful Grounded Yoga about page, boutique studio" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f3b} alt="Graceful Grounded Yoga homepage section" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
            <Image class="freelance-thumb" src={f4a} alt="Bass Coast Podiatry homepage, health services" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[600,900]} sizes="280px"/>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="scroll-hint">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          Scroll to see more
        </p>
      </section>

    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
.case-page{position:relative;width:min(calc(100% - 3rem),78rem);margin:0 auto;padding:1.25rem 0 5rem}
.eyebrow{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0 0 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center}
.breadcrumb-link{font-weight:600}.breadcrumb-separator{color:var(--muted-foreground)}
h1,h2{margin:0;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.05em;color:var(--foreground)}
.display-title{font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.06;margin:1rem 0 1.5rem;max-width:28ch}
.hero-subtext{font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted-foreground);font-style:italic;margin:.25rem 0 0;max-width:42rem}
.hero-text,.story-block p,.summary-main p{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 1rem}
.case-hero{padding:5rem 0 2rem}
.meta-strip{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2rem;padding:1.5rem 0 .5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.meta-label{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0}
.meta-value{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700}
.lead-image-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem}
.lead-image,.supporting-image,.pair-image{width:100%;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1.5rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-large)}
.pair-image-constrained{width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1.5rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-large)}
.supporting-image-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.img-pair-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.img-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.5rem}
.summary-section{padding:0 0 3rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.summary-section h2{margin-top:.75rem;font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.5vw,2.2rem);max-width:32ch}
.summary-main{margin-top:1.5rem;max-width:44rem}
.section-kicker{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0 0 .5rem}
.editorial-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:14rem minmax(0,1fr);gap:2rem;padding:3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.story-block{max-width:44rem}
.freelance-section{padding:3.5rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.freelance-section h2{margin:.5rem 0 0;font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.5vw,2rem)}
.freelance-intro{font-size:1rem;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:.75rem 0 1.75rem;max-width:42rem;line-height:1.7}
.freelance-scroll{overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;padding-bottom:1rem;margin:0 -2rem;padding-left:2rem;padding-right:2rem}
.freelance-track{display:flex;gap:1.25rem;width:max-content}
.freelance-thumb{width:840px;height:570px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);box-shadow:0 8px 20px rgba(23,23,23,.07);flex-shrink:0}
.scroll-hint{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-top:.75rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.75rem;color:var(--muted-foreground);letter-spacing:.04em}
.scroll-hint svg{width:1.25rem;height:1.25rem;opacity:.6}
@media(max-width:860px){.img-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}.editorial-section{grid-template-columns:1fr}.freelance-thumb{width:320px;height:215px}}
</style>
